{"status":"ok","message-type":"work-list","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"facets":{},"total-results":11434348,"items":[{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2025,5,14]],"date-time":"2025-05-14T08:07:24Z","timestamp":1747210044294,"version":"3.40.5"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Universidad Autonoma Metropolitana","issue":"02","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["AZCATL"],"abstract":"<jats:p>Throughout the course of history, solar eclipses have had a scientific and cultural impact in human society. On Oc-tober 14th 2023 and April 8th 2024 two solar eclipses were visible from M\u00e9xico and the Universidad Aut\u00f3noma Metropolitana, Unidad Azcapotzalco documented both. Through this experience, we invite the community to ponder on the relevance these events have together with their corresponding utility and the way in which the interested reader can become an eclipse hunter <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.24275\/azcatl2024a001","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2024,8,6]],"date-time":"2024-08-06T23:10:43Z","timestamp":1722985843000},"page":"04-10","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["A la cacer\u00eda de Eclipses solares"],"prefix":"10.24275","volume":"01","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-0378-0415","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"C\u00e9sar Sim\u00f3n","family":"L\u00f3pez Monsalvo","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Divisi\u00f3n de Ciencias B\u00e1sicas e Ingenier\u00eda, Universidad Aut\u00f3noma Metropolina, Unidad Azcapotzlco"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Gabriela Isabel","family":"Vera Garf\u00edas","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Divisi\u00f3n de Ciencias B\u00e1sicas e Ingenier\u00eda, Universidad Aut\u00f3noma Metropolina, Unidad Azcapotzlco"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-7562-2918","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Alberto","family":"Rubio Ponce","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"BDivisi\u00f3n de Ciencias B\u00e1sicas e Ingenier\u00eda, Universidad Aut\u00f3noma Metropolina, Unidad Azcapotzlco"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Sergio","family":"Islas Ram\u00edrez","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-5691-9329","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Jos\u00e9 Luis","family":"Hern\u00e1ndez \u00c1vila","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Divisi\u00f3n de Ciencias B\u00e1sicas e Ingenier\u00eda, Universidad Aut\u00f3noma Metropolina, Unidad Azcapotzlco"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"10370","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2024,7,31]]},"container-title":["AZCATL"],"original-title":["A la cacer\u00eda de Eclipses solares"],"language":"en","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2024,8,6]],"date-time":"2024-08-06T23:10:45Z","timestamp":1722985845000},"score":74.07444,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/azcatl.azc.uam.mx\/index.php\/azcatl\/article\/view\/41\/48"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024,7,31]]},"references-count":0,"journal-issue":{"issue":"02","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2024,7,31]]}},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.24275\/azcatl2024a001","published":{"date-parts":[[2024,7,31]]}},{"institution":[{"name":"Universidad Aut\u00f3noma Metropolitana (M\u00e9xico). Unidad Azcapotzalco.","acronym":["UAMA"],"place":["Ciudad de M\u00e9xico"],"department":["Ciencias B\u00e1sicas e Ingenier\u00eda."]}],"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2025,10,29]],"date-time":"2025-10-29T17:30:26Z","timestamp":1761759026759,"version":"build-2065373602"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Universidad Autonoma Metropolitana","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"chair":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-0378-0415","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"C\u00e9sar Sim\u00f3n","family":"L\u00f3pez Monsalvo","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"chair","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-7562-2918","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Alberto","family":"Rubio Ponce","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"chair","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"abstract":"<jats:p>This study pioneers a covariant formulation of Ohm\u2019s law, melding differential geometry with the principles of special relativity to resolve long-standing inconsistencies in classical electromagnetic theory. Traditional Newtonian models fail to align with the inherent symmetries of electromagnetism and relativity, creating a pressing need for a more comprehensive approach. By focusing on the often-overlooked role of the observer and employing advanced geometric tools, this research provides a profound understanding of electrical conduction across various conditions. For over a century, microscopic theories have successfully derived Ohm\u2019s law from thermodynamic principles. However, these models, rooted in Newtonian physics, imply instantaneous propagation\u2014a notion incompatible with relativistic principles. This study introduces a covariant model that respects the symmetries of electromagnetism and highlights the critical role of the observer, addressing gaps left by classical formulations. The geometric approach adopted here emphasizes the observer\u2019s central role, providing clearer interpretations of experimental data and theoretical predictions. This research bridges the gap between classical and modern electromagnetic theories, offering practical insights for the design of advanced electromagnetic systems and material science applications. By ensuring coordinate and observer independence, the model underscores the inherent symmetries in physical laws, offering a robust framework for understanding electrical conduction in relativistic contexts.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.24275\/uama.6741.12640","type":"dissertation","created":{"date-parts":[[2025,10,29]],"date-time":"2025-10-29T17:27:36Z","timestamp":1761758856000},"approved":{"date-parts":[[2024,9,23]]},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["La geometr\u00eda de los medios conductores en movimiento"],"prefix":"10.24275","author":[{"sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0001-2977-1517","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Uriel","family":"Aguilar Fern\u00e1ndez","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"10370","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/hdl.handle.net\/11191\/12640","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2025,10,29]],"date-time":"2025-10-29T17:27:37Z","timestamp":1761758857000},"score":31.607967,"degree":["Maestr\u00eda."],"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/zaloamati.azc.uam.mx\/handle\/11191\/12640"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[null]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.24275\/uama.6741.12640"},{"institution":[{"name":"Universidad Aut\u00f3noma Metropolitana. Unidad Azcapotzalco.","acronym":["UAMA"],"place":["Ciudad de M\u00e9xico"],"department":["Divisi\u00f3n de Ciencias B\u00e1sicas e Ingenier\u00eda"]}],"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2025,5,14]],"date-time":"2025-05-14T08:08:53Z","timestamp":1747210133390,"version":"3.40.5"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Universidad Autonoma Metropolitana","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"chair":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-0378-0415","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"C\u00e9sar Sim\u00f3n","family":"L\u00f3pez Monsalvo","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"chair","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-7562-2918","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Alberto","family":"Rubio Ponce","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"chair","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"abstract":"<jats:p>Este trabajo pretende abordar los fundamentos geom\u00e9tricos de la propagaci\u00f3n de la luz en medios para entender la \u00f3ptica de transformaciones y poder generar una base sobre la cual, de manera can\u00f3nica, se puedan dise\u00f1ar nuevos materiales. Para tal efecto la tesis se encuentra estructurada de la siguiente manera. En el cap\u00edtulo 3, exponemos las bases del electromagnetismo vectorial y su contraparte en formas diferenciales, haciendo expl\u00edcita la conversi\u00f3n de un lenguaje a otro. Planteamos las relaciones constitutivas de forma completamente geom\u00e9trica, y desarrollamos la manera de encontrar las componentes de los campos electromagn\u00e9ticos inducidos independientes del observador y del marco en referencia. Esta metodolog\u00eda la extendemos a medios en movimiento y proponemos medios est\u00e1ticos equivalentes. Trabajamos con conductores y escribimos la versi\u00f3n geom\u00e9trica de la ley de Ohm. Definimos una 3-forma de densidad de flujo de energ\u00eda-momento con la cual damos una versi\u00f3n geom\u00e9trica del teorema de Poynting. En el cap\u00edtulo 4, mostramos una manera de encontrar los diferentes tensores de permitividad, permeabilidad y las matrices magnetoel\u00e9ctricas en t\u00e9rminos de un tensor constitutivo. Exponemos los fundamentos de la m\u00e9trica \u00f3ptica y la usamos para realizar diferentes ejemplos de medios equivalentes a geometr\u00edas cosmol\u00f3gicas conocidas. En el cap\u00edtulo 5 damos las bases matem\u00e1ticas de la geometr\u00eda de contacto partiendo desde la perspectiva de las ecuaciones diferenciales. Con este lenguaje geom\u00e9trico escribimos la evoluci\u00f3n de la luz tanto en t\u00e9rminos de rayos como en frentes de ondas. Finalmente, construimos el principio de Huygens usando los diferentes espacios matem\u00e1ticos previamente definidos y demostramos con geometr\u00eda, que la evoluci\u00f3n de un frente de onda es la envolvente de los frentes de ondas secundarios producidos. En el cap\u00edtulo 6, ahondamos en las estructuras de los espacios matem\u00e1ticos que subyacen en las diferentes formas de evolucionar la luz en un medio. El haz tangente unitario para un rayo de luz y el espacio de elementos de contacto para la visi\u00f3n ondulatoria. En el cap\u00edtulo se muestra de manera expl\u00edcita la equivalencia geom\u00e9trica de los principios de Fermat y de Huygens y se encuentra que tanto el flujo geod\u00e9sico como los frentes de onda, pueden ser reconstruidos a partir de encontrar la familia uniparam\u00e9trica de transformaci\u00f3n de contacto, asociadas al flujo del campo vectorial de Reeb de la forma de contacto de Liouville. Este formalismo, permite recrear tanto las trayectorias de los rayos de luz, sin la necesidad de resolver la ecuaci\u00f3n geod\u00e9sica para la variedad (ecuaci\u00f3n diferencial de 2\u00ba grado) y permite a su vez reconstruir los frentes de onda, sin resolver de manera directa la ecuaci\u00f3n de onda (ecuaci\u00f3n diferencial de 2\u00ba grado). Todo esto se logra encontrando un flujo vectorial que es una ecuaci\u00f3n diferencial de 1\u00ba orden. Realizamos una serie de ejemplos, para medios con geometr\u00eda trivial y no trivial y diferentes dimensiones. En el cap\u00edtulo 7 definimos las formas diferenciales de Beltrami en analog\u00eda a los campos vectoriales de Beltrami. Partimos de estos campos para definir la helicidad en el contexto de las formas diferenciales, as\u00ed como otros invariantes topol\u00f3gicos asociados. Usamos estos conceptos para definir la geometr\u00eda de un superconductor en 2 dimensiones espaciales y deducimos las ecuaciones de London en su forma geom\u00e9trica. Finalmente, en el cap\u00edtulo 8 damos las conclusiones del trabajo, as\u00ed como algunos otros trabajos que se encuentran en elaboraci\u00f3n.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.24275\/uama.6738.9686","type":"dissertation","created":{"date-parts":[[2023,6,1]],"date-time":"2023-06-01T01:04:07Z","timestamp":1685581447000},"approved":{"date-parts":[[2023,5,22]]},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Sobre los fundamentos geom\u00e9tricos de la propagaci\u00f3n de la luz en medios"],"prefix":"10.24275","author":[{"sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-9701-0947","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"David","family":"Garc\u00eda Pel\u00e1ez Cruz","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"10370","link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/hdl.handle.net\/11191\/9686","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2023,6,1]],"date-time":"2023-06-01T01:04:10Z","timestamp":1685581450000},"score":31.212534,"degree":["Doctorado"],"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"http:\/\/zaloamati.azc.uam.mx\/handle\/11191\/9686"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[null]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.24275\/uama.6738.9686"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,23]],"date-time":"2026-10-23T01:38:15Z","timestamp":1792719495318,"version":"4.5.0"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Universidad Nacional de Trujillo","issue":"3","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Sci. agropecu"],"abstract":"<jats:p>La caza es una actividad de subsistencia importante en regiones con bosques tropicales. La carne silvestre es fuente de alimento e ingreso para amplios sectores de la poblaci\u00f3n, siendo parte relevante de las econom\u00edas locales. La extracci\u00f3n excesiva de fauna silvestre afecta a diversas especies, incluso llev\u00e1ndolas hasta la extinci\u00f3n. La oferta y la demanda juegan un rol fundamental en los niveles de extracci\u00f3n de carne silvestre, teniendo los precios una significativa influencia sobre los niveles de caza. Tanto el mercado como la interdicci\u00f3n deben actuar juntos para lograr una extracci\u00f3n sostenible y la protecci\u00f3n de la fauna silvestre. Es urgente dise\u00f1ar pol\u00edticas de manejo que sean realistas y aplicables, tomando en consideraci\u00f3n los aspectos sociales, e incluyendo el monitoreo y la promoci\u00f3n de la conservaci\u00f3n del recurso. El objetivo de la presente revisi\u00f3n es dar a conocer la problem\u00e1tica en torno al consumo de carne de origen silvestre en regiones con bosque tropical, resaltar la influencia de factores socioecon\u00f3micos en la intensidad de extracci\u00f3n y presentar la informaci\u00f3n para su difusi\u00f3n.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.17268\/sci.agropecu.2019.03.15","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2019,10,14]],"date-time":"2019-10-14T15:24:51Z","timestamp":1571066691000},"page":"433-448","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":5,"title":["El mercado de la cacer\u00eda \u2013 la cacer\u00eda del mercado: carne de origen silvestre en bosques tropicales"],"prefix":"10.17268","volume":"10","author":[{"given":"Diego","family":"Shoobridge","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Universidad Nacional Agraria La Molina."}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"6846","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2019,10,7]]},"container-title":["Scientia Agropecuaria"],"link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/revistas.unitru.edu.pe\/index.php\/scientiaagrop\/article\/download\/2565\/2623","content-type":"application\/pdf","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/revistas.unitru.edu.pe\/index.php\/scientiaagrop\/article\/download\/2565\/3150","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/revistas.unitru.edu.pe\/index.php\/scientiaagrop\/article\/download\/2565\/2623","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,23]],"date-time":"2026-10-23T01:08:34Z","timestamp":1792717714000},"score":29.120823,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/revistas.unitru.edu.pe\/index.php\/scientiaagrop\/article\/view\/2565"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2019,10,7]]},"references-count":0,"journal-issue":{"issue":"3","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2019,10,7]]}},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.17268\/sci.agropecu.2019.03.15","ISSN":["2306-6741","2077-9917"],"issn-type":[{"value":"2306-6741","type":"electronic"},{"value":"2077-9917","type":"print"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2019,10,7]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,7]],"date-time":"2026-08-07T16:54:44Z","timestamp":1786121684386,"version":"build-2736575974"},"reference-count":57,"publisher":"Autonomous University of Yucatan","issue":"55\/enero-julio","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,14]],"date-time":"2026-04-14T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1776124800000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by-nc\/4.0"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Tohil"],"abstract":"<jats:p>The manuscript analyzes the experience of the agroecological collective Solares, formed by Maya women from Sotuta, Yucat\u00e1n, to identify the extent to which their practices align with a model of women's solidarity economy and the strategies they generate in response to extractive pressures in their territory. The study uses a qualitative approach and combines seven months of participant observation with four in-depth interviews conducted with founding members of the project. The information was coded with ATLAS.ti 25 and organized through an interpretive framework centered on the situated experiences of the women. The results show that the recovery of the Maya solar produces an economic rationality grounded in the sustenance of life, daily cooperation, and productive diversification. Agricultural practices rely on local knowledge, intergenerational transmission, and continuous management of time and resources. The collective strengthens the women\u2019s productive identity, shared work organization, and horizontal decision-making. The project also generates income, food, medicinal products, and a space for mutual support.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.32776\/ja7bj289","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,15]],"date-time":"2026-04-15T00:45:27Z","timestamp":1776213927000},"page":"e002","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Del extractivismo a la econom\u00eda solidaria","From extractivism to the solidarity economy: the case of Maya women of Sotuta and the agroecological collective Solares"],"prefix":"10.32776","volume":"28","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-7497-2986","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Edwin Alberto","family":"Fern\u00e1ndez Sarabia","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-3879-3360","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Roc\u00edo","family":"Quintal L\u00f3pez","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"17934","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,14]]},"reference":[{"key":"4142","unstructured":"ACOSTA, Alberto, \u201cExtractivismo y neoextractivismo: dos caras de la misma maldici\u00f3n\u201d, en Extractivismo, pol\u00edtica y sociedad, CAAP; CLAES, 2012, pp. 101\u2013125."},{"key":"4143","unstructured":"CARRASCO, Cristina (ed.), Con voz propia: La econom\u00eda feminista como apuesta te\u00f3rica y pol\u00edtica, Viento Sur, 2014."},{"key":"4144","unstructured":"ESCOBAR, Arturo, Sentipensar con la tierra: Nuevas lecturas sobre desarrollo, territorio y diferencia, Ediciones UNAULA, 2014."},{"key":"4145","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"HARVEY, David, The New Imperialism, Oxford University Press, 2003.","DOI":"10.1093\/oso\/9780199264315.001.0001"},{"key":"4146","unstructured":"MARA\u00d1\u00d3N, Boris (coord.), La econom\u00eda solidaria en M\u00